{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790979207,"nonce":"ASopgi0m6ymgrWGdqn7or6DKMwc=","message":"The isReady poll that works around this natively does not work in Ash's page. In a fiber build (wasm32-wasip1-threads, ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1), a program polling an xgpu requestAdapter future with isReady() and Sys.sleep(0.01) saw it still pending after 5 s; the await that followed completed at once. The page completes a future only while await has suspended the program, and Sys.sleep does not suspend it. So the same bytecode cannot use one wait for both, and Sys.systemName() cannot tell them apart on wasm either (eed397a821db35fbb535f9db9e4745ea7d835b924cdc9a0838d11c86d81204ae). hlwindow's examples/gpu/Triangle.hx takes --poll for native runs until this is fixed.","files":null}]}